# The line endings are the repository's, not the checkout's.
#
# Without this, Git for Windows checks every text file out as CRLF, because
# `core.autocrlf=true` is what its installer sets by default. That is a fight
# nobody wins here, and the six files it is lost on are these:
#
#   linux/flutter/generated_plugin_registrant.cc
#   linux/flutter/generated_plugin_registrant.h
#   linux/flutter/generated_plugins.cmake
#   windows/flutter/generated_plugin_registrant.cc
#   windows/flutter/generated_plugin_registrant.h
#   windows/flutter/generated_plugins.cmake
#
# Those are written by the Flutter tool, which renders its template and writes
# the string it rendered — with LF, on every platform, and with no conversion
# of any kind. So Git checks them out as CRLF, the next `flutter run` puts
# them back to LF, and they are reported as modified for the rest of time even
# though not one byte of their content ever changes.
#
# `eol=lf` settles it: LF in the repository and LF in the working tree, on
# every machine, whatever the local `core.autocrlf` says. Every file tracked
# here was already LF when this was written, so it normalises nothing — it
# only stops the conversion that was never wanted.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The ones that are not text, marked rather than left to be sniffed.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
